cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reference model or its derived application mappings, please cite this release and the underlying DIO/ODI publications."
title: "DIO/ODI Reference Model"
type: software
version: "0.6.0"
abstract: "Release candidate 0.6.0 of the versioned DIO/ODI reference model centered on a machine-readable SKOS vocabulary for Digital Identity Optimization (DIO) and Ontology of Digital Identity (ODI), with stable concept URIs, provenance, Turtle and JSON-LD serializations, concept maps, and explicitly separated derived application mappings. This snapshot incorporates Reference Vocabulary v0.2.0, including a distinct plural Identity-Preserving Constraints concept while retaining the singular URI as a historical entry without asserting a semantic relation between them. It carries forward the HEM × DIO, Commit-Boundary × Policy-as-Code, and iterative/hypothesis-conditioned RAG mappings, and adds the non-normative Agentic ER Commit-Boundary Architecture Mapping v0.3.0 with 120 local concepts and 206 qualified relation assertions."
authors:
